usage: install.py [-h] [--source SOURCE] [--source-manifest SOURCE_MANIFEST]
                  [--commit COMMIT] [--version VERSION]
                  [--request-file REQUEST_FILE] [--operation-id OPERATION_ID]
                  [--agent {codex,claude,workbuddy}]
                  [--approval-file APPROVAL_FILE] [--recover RECOVER]
                  [--action {continue,rollback}] [--acquire]
                  [--staging STAGING] [--project PROJECT] [--context-keeper]
                  [--ck-source CK_SOURCE]

Machine installation: preview first; execute only an exact approved plan.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --source SOURCE       Absolute clean local Git checkout (default: this
                        source checkout)
  --source-manifest SOURCE_MANIFEST
                        Absolute JSON file containing a verified source object
  --commit COMMIT       Full pinned source commit; local default is current
                        verified HEAD
  --version VERSION     Target product code version MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
  --request-file REQUEST_FILE
                        Absolute JSON: conversions/legacy ledger
                        identity/evidence inputs
  --operation-id OPERATION_ID
  --agent {codex,claude,workbuddy}
  --approval-file APPROVAL_FILE
                        Absolute JSON exact plan plus confirmed_at/reference
  --recover RECOVER     Absolute operation journal; independent recovery mode
  --action {continue,rollback}
                        Recovery action
  --acquire             Separate official pinned-source acquisition plan
  --staging STAGING     Absolute absent acquisition directory
  --project PROJECT     Actual absolute project root for reported follow-up
                        commands only
  --context-keeper      Independent optional CK user-install plan
  --ck-source CK_SOURCE
                        Absolute durable clean CK checkout at the integration
                        pin
